WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.934 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-I'm very impressed that

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
you use your time off
from your television job

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:03.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
to come do stage work.
-Uh-huh. I do.

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:05.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Last time you were here,
you were doing a one-man show,

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:06.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Fully Committed."
-Yes. Yes.

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:08.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, this time, you're
actually sharing the stage

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:10.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
with some other actors.
-There's a few other actors.

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:13.613
The last one, I played
40 characters in a one-man show,

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:15.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, this time,
I'm playing one character

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:17.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
in a play with six people.
-Okay. So that's --

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:19.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's more -- That's --
I like that more.

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:21.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You like that more. Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:22.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I can imagine
playing 40 characters

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:24.457
for however many nights you
did it was pretty exhausting.

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:25.091 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It was great.

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:27.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I lost like 15 pounds
during the run.

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:29.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you want to lose weight,
just do a one-man show.

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:30.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.
-It's really...

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:32.399
-That's what they all say.
-That's what they all say.

00:00:32.399 --> 00:00:34.100 line:92%
-This is an interesting play

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
about the different
kind of people

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:36.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
that can start families...
-Right.

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:38.505
-..and how they start families.
-Yeah.

00:00:38.505 --> 00:00:40.407 size:78% position:39%
And it's sort of like
about the breakdown

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:42.108 line:92%
of the, you know, empathy

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:44.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
between subcultures
of the LGBTQ community.

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:46.646 size:81% position:41%
And I -- That sounds
really dry and boring,

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:48.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it's actually
a really funny play,

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:49.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there are a lot of moments
where, like,

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:50.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I can't believe you just said
that, but you did."

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:52.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you actually learn --
I'm learning a lot

00:00:52.986 --> 00:00:54.187 line:92%
about the transgender community.

00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:56.623
And it's -- it's a really
great play, very timely.

00:00:56.623 --> 00:00:58.258
-Well, that's helpful, because,
you know,

00:00:58.258 --> 00:01:00.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
I do think there are things
we could all --

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:02.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
all want to learn
about different communities,

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:04.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
and sometimes
we are afraid that,

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:06.199 line:92%
if we ask, we'll seem ignorant.

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:07.100 line:92%
-Yeah, I had friends who came,

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.302
and, like, we ask some of these
questions in the play,

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:10.003 line:92%
and my friends were like,

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:11.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, we want to know
the answer to that, too."

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:12.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.
-Like, truly --

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:14.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, "I've always been scared
to ask that question."

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:15.542 size:81% position:41% line:92%
So it's -- it's great.

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:16.876 line:92%
-You are introduced in the play

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:20.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
as a gay uncle who's
in charge of babysitting.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:21.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
You do some babysitting.
-Yes.

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:23.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Yes.

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:25.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
I used to babys-- that
was like my bread and butter

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:27.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
before I became
a successful actor.

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:29.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light laughter ]
-Wow.

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:30.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
Were you good?
Were you --

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:32.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was an amazing babysitter.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:32.959 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-You really were? Okay.

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:34.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I really was
a great babysitter.

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:36.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
I babysat for a friend of mine
who was an actor,

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:39.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I had just, you know,
his daughter Nora,

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:40.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I would take her to, like,
in the parks,

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:42.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I would meet other parents
while I was at the parks.

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:45.004
And they would kind of be like,
"Who's that guy?

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:47.674
Can -- Do you -- Do you have --
Do you do this a lot?

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:49.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do -- Do you have time, like,
on Thursday?

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:52.178
Can you come by?
Like, we're short a babysitter."

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:54.447
And so I started getting poached
by other parents.

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:55.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
-And then I started,

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:57.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, hedging them
against one another.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:00.120
It's like, "Well,
Mrs. Morrison pays $12 an hour."

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
So, like, you know --

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:03.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was really --
I was quite a shark.

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:04.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
-Yeah.

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:06.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's very impressive.
-Uh-huh. Yeah.

00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:07.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I'm also...
-And not to say

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:10.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
I won't go back to it
when "Modern Family" is done.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:11.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean...
-Yeah.

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:12.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Chuckles ]
If anyone wants me to...

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:15.635
[ Cheers and applause ]
-But let's make it clear.

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:16.836 line:92%
-Yeah, my rates have gone up.

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:18.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's not 12 bucks anymore,
yeah.

00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:20.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Let's talk about inflation.
Yeah.

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:23.009 line:92%
-Do you like using your off time

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:24.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
from being
in front of a TV camera

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:26.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
to come back and do theater?
-I do. I love it.

00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:27.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, with --
when you're on camera --

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:30.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you know this
from doing TV --

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:31.217 size:75% position:38% line:92%
like, you -- your --

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:32.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
your performance is edited
in another room.

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:36.723
And, like, in theater, you know,
you're in complete charge --

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:38.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
in control of your --
your performance.

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:39.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think it's so exciting.
-And it's great.

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:43.263
And you can adjust based on
the audience on any given night.

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:43.997 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Yeah, yeah, absolutely.

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:44.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, you're not laughing
right now,

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:46.966
so, then, I would do, like,
something wacky like this,

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:48.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then you'd start laughing.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.635 --> 00:02:50.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, you know,
you can do things like that.

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:50.970 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-You got them.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:53.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you can wave to Fred
when you're feeling insecure.

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:53.940 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he doesn't wave back,
but that's fine.

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:58.011
That's fine. It's fine.
It's like, don't worry about it.

00:02:58.011 --> 00:02:58.778 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:58.778 --> 00:03:01.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Fred.
-[ Speaking indistinctly ]

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:05.585 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:07.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You -- You and your husband
just traveled.

00:03:07.387 --> 00:03:08.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You went to London.

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:10.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
You went to Paris.
-And Berlin.

00:03:10.423 --> 00:03:11.491
-Berlin.
-Which I'd never been to before.

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:12.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How is Berlin?
-It's great.

00:03:12.492 --> 00:03:14.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's great for people
who are willing

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:16.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
to, like, see the sunrise.
-Yeah.

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:17.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Which --
I'm not one of those people.

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:18.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
I really like sleep.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:21.201
-I went to Berlin once, and
I think I went a little late.

00:03:21.201 --> 00:03:23.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, my party days were over,
and I felt like an old man.

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:25.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah. Mine, too.
Absolutely, I'm with you.

00:03:25.338 --> 00:03:27.540
We should go to Berlin together.
-Yeah. Great.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I -- We --
-Did you make an effort?

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:30.210 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-We did make an effort.

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:33.279
One night, we definitely made it
to like 8:00 a.m.

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:34.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah.
-That's great.

00:03:34.414 --> 00:03:36.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-And...

00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:37.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
we were really proud
of ourselves,

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:40.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then, we basically fell
asleep for a whole day

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:41.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
and lost a day in Berlin.
-Yeah.

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:42.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-That's not great.

00:03:42.589 --> 00:03:45.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So it wasn't fully worth it,
to be honest.

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:48.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You did not go to the Tonys.
-No.

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:49.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, I was doing --
I was onstage that night.

00:03:49.696 --> 00:03:51.764 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right, so, but you did go
to Tonys after parties.

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:54.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I went to the after parties,
which I think is probably

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:55.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
the way to do it now.
-Yeah.

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:57.337
-Just, like, skip the ceremony,
and go to the parties.

00:03:57.337 --> 00:04:00.607
And, again, I was kind of trying
to relive my Berlin days.

00:04:00.607 --> 00:04:02.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was, like,
staying out way too late.

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:03.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, no.
-Yeah, it was --

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:04.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But you just found out
from Berlin

00:04:04.844 --> 00:04:05.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you're not cut for that.
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:08.648
-How did you forget so quickly?
-I just forgot very quickly.

00:04:08.648 --> 00:04:10.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
Enough liquor
makes you forget things.

00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:11.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:12.852 line:92%
-And I knew it was time to leave

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:15.355 size:75% position:38%
when my friend Colin
brought me back --

00:04:15.355 --> 00:04:17.056 line:92%
I had been drinking vodka sodas,

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:18.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he brought me back
a drink that --

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:21.761
it was a tequila and water
with no ice in a Martini glass,

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:23.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he's like,
"This is all they have left."

00:04:23.563 --> 00:04:24.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
I was like,

00:04:24.664 --> 00:04:25.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Then we need to go home."
-Yeah.

00:04:25.999 --> 00:04:27.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like, that's when you leave.
-Right.

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:30.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"We can't be here anymore."
-Yeah, you can stay --

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:32.672
you can keep drinking your first
choice and your second choice.

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:33.506 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:34.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But when
it's the last choice...

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:35.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it's warm...
-Yeah.

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:38.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...and in a Martini glass,
and it doesn't belong in that,

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:39.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's just --
it's time to go home.

00:04:39.479 --> 00:04:40.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:40.146 --> 00:04:41.848
-It's like, "I can give you
a pint of rosé..." Unh-unh.

00:04:41.848 --> 00:04:43.616 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, in, like, a sippy cup.
You're like,

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:46.352
"I don't feel like this is what
I should be doing right now."

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:48.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I didn't realize this --
which is an incredible pull --

00:04:48.621 --> 00:04:51.491
Tony Kushner, the incredible
playwright, married you guys.

00:04:51.491 --> 00:04:53.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
Yeah, he was our officiant.

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:54.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, he wrote
"Angels in America"

00:04:54.594 --> 00:04:55.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
and is a Pulitzer Prize winner
for that.

00:04:55.728 --> 00:04:56.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:56.696 --> 00:04:59.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And...yeah.
-And, of course...

00:04:59.065 --> 00:05:03.803
he -- you know, he deservedly --
that show won a Tony this year.

00:05:03.803 --> 00:05:05.171 line:92%
-Yeah, they won tons of Tonys.

00:05:05.171 --> 00:05:07.006 line:92%
-Have you seen the revival?

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:09.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I have seen it.
I loved it.

00:05:09.042 --> 00:05:11.110 line:92%
I was highly impressed with it.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:12.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nathan Lane, of course,
is in it.

00:05:12.178 --> 00:05:13.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he's -- he plays Pepper
on "Modern Family."

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:17.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I was there to see him,
and it's so amazing seeing him

00:05:17.383 --> 00:05:19.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
in a role
that's completely different

00:05:19.085 --> 00:05:20.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
from the role he plays on
"Modern Family."

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:22.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did you see it same day,
back to back?

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:23.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did two days.
I needed --

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:24.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had to sleep in between.
-Got you.

00:05:24.857 --> 00:05:26.326 size:75% position:38%
-Some people do this
throughout one day,

00:05:26.326 --> 00:05:26.993 line:92%
and I was like, I feel --

00:05:26.993 --> 00:05:28.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel better going to bed
between plays.

00:05:28.594 --> 00:05:31.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, but you did do them
back-to-back days?

00:05:31.531 --> 00:05:32.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
You did have a --
-Yes. Yeah, yeah.

00:05:32.532 --> 00:05:33.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
Absolutely, yeah.
-That's really cool.

00:05:33.599 --> 00:05:35.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, I mean, it was --
it was fantastic.

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:37.003 line:92%
It's an amazing production

00:05:37.003 --> 00:05:38.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
that people should
definitely try and catch.

00:05:38.938 --> 00:05:41.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's amazing that
you pulled Tony Kushner

00:05:41.974 --> 00:05:43.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
as an officiant
for your wedding.

00:05:43.343 --> 00:05:44.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I just asked him,
and he said, "Yes,"

00:05:44.877 --> 00:05:46.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is --
I mean, I kind of knew him,

00:05:46.746 --> 00:05:49.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
but not well enough to say,
"Will you marry us?"

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:49.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And I was like,

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:51.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Well, I'm gonna just try."
And he said, "Okay."

00:05:51.951 --> 00:05:54.487
And, like, we basically had,
like, a breakfast together

00:05:54.487 --> 00:05:56.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
where he, like,
asked us how we met.

00:05:56.155 --> 00:05:57.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like,
"This is just so weird."

00:05:57.557 --> 00:05:58.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
